# Project

Purpose:
  Project model registry and routing table. Defines the SHAPE of how
  projects are structured — Project > Domain > Module > Feature >
  Component hierarchy — and routes to model files.

  This folder contains MODEL and SCHEMA only — no concrete project data.
  Concrete project instances live under .sdd/projects/<name>/.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1  @project.sdd
   2  @domains.sdd
   3  @modules.sdd
   4  @flows.sdd
   5  @dependencies.sdd
   6  @instantiation.sdd
   7  @map.sdd
   8  @architecture.sdd

Rules:
  [PM1] This folder defines reusable project structure schemas only.
  [PM2] Concrete project instances MUST live under .sdd/projects/<name>/.
  [PM3] AI MUST NOT place project state in this folder.
  [PM4] Domain and module schemas are templates; concrete instances belong to instantiated project.
  [PM5] Indexes are routing metadata, not source of truth.
  [PM6] Indexes MUST reference authoritative SDD files, not duplicate them.

Indexes:
  module, domain, feature, api, database, dependency, test, deployment

Navigation:
  ProjectModel: @project.sdd
  Domains: @domains.sdd
  Modules: @modules.sdd
  Flows: @flows.sdd
  Dependencies: @dependencies.sdd
  Instantiation: @instantiation.sdd
  Map: @map.sdd
  Architecture: @architecture.sdd
  Projects: @../projects/INDEX.sdd
  Root: @../INDEX.sdd

State: +